  "text_pages": [
    "Exchange/Visiting Pre-Arrival Guide - d. Scholarships\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nFinancial Support & Scholarships\nExchange Students\nThe\ntwo\nscholarships listed below are\nONLY\naccessible to\nExchange students.\nScholarships are NOT always available; they are subject to government/univeristy funding availability. We will let you know if there is any availability; there is no need to ask!\nGlobal Korea Scholarship (GKS)\nFunded by the Korean Government for Foreign Exchange Students\nThis scholarship program is organized to provide continual opportunities for international exchange students to study in Korea and delve into Korean culture. Any international student with academic merit is eligible to apply for this scholarship program. All incoming exchange students are automatically considered as candidates for screening and there is no separate application form.\nHUFS will select the top-qualified students within the given number of slots for each year.\nNumber of slots for 2024 Recommendation: 8 recipients\nEligibility & Conditions\nStudents should be officially nominated by our international partner universities.\nStudents should take at least one regular semester course related to Korea during the exchange program.\nStudents are required to provide evidence (academic transcript) of grade point averages over 3.2 out of 4.0.\nCurrent exchange students are not eligible to apply for this program.\nOnly undergraduate students are eligible to apply for this scholarship program.\nApplication Procedures\nExchange students should submit their exchange application before the application deadline.\nHUFS and NIIED (National Institute for International Education) will screen & evaluate all applications received at the time of application to the exchange program.\nFinal scholarship winners will be announced in late February/August on this website.\nScholarship Benefits\nAirfare reimbursement (round-trip)\nMonthly stipend of KRW 630,000\nPeer Tutoring Scholarship\nThe Peer Tutoring program is an opportunity for international students to exchange language and culture with full-time HUFS students. Tutees (international students) will be requried to deliver 7.5 - 10 hours of language exchange to tutors (full-time HUFS students). The language offered to be taught each semester changes depending on the demand from full-time HUFS students each year. Eligible candidates will be contacted separately with the opportunity.\nScholarship Amount\n: 250,000 KRW - 500,000 KRW\nApplication\n: Through the Office of International Admissions & Management\nNote\nOnly native speakers of offered language can apply\nIf selected as a tutor, you will meet with Korean students once a week to share your language and culture. You will also do a project together.\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  ],
